# Logs. Anchored to the repo root — a bare `logs` pattern matches any path
# component named "logs" anywhere in the tree, which was silently swallowing
# the Logs feature's own source directories (src/pages/logs, src/lib/logs).
/logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?
/CLAUDE.md
.claude/

# Raw FAA NASR subscription cycles — ~600MB per cycle, re-downloadable from
# faa.gov, and superseded every 28 days. Only the GeoJSON derived from it is
# committed. Ignore the contents but keep the README that says which cycle to
# fetch and how to regenerate — that has to survive a clone.
/data/nasr/*
!/data/nasr/README.md

# Class E is 4,327 polygons / 15MB — 85% of the derived airspace output, and
# committing it each 28-day cycle would add ~200MB a year of permanent history
# for the class least likely to gate a launch. B/C/D (2.6MB) are committed;
# run `npm run build:airspace` to generate this one locally. The map treats a
# missing layer file as unavailable rather than an error, and the View menu
# shows it as "not built".
/public/airspace/class-e.json

# Updater signing keypair (private key + password). Only the public key
# (copied into tauri.conf.json) is meant to be committed — the private key
# and password belong in GitHub Actions secrets, never in the repo.
/.secrets/
